        "id": 11550,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-16T06:46:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was playing a game today in Time Cataclysm where Parse had her Buffer Overflow up, and Fixed Point was out. So, does she get to discard villian cards for free? Fixed point states:</p><blockquote><p>&nbsp;<span>When a villain card would enter play, you may discard it instead and destroy this card.</span></p><p><span>When this card is destroyed, draw a card and play the top card of the villain deck.</span></p></blockquote><p>I realize discarding is not destroying, and the first part would play as normal. The only issue I'm seeing is a simultaneous action of discarding and destroying, and if one can't be fulfilled, the entire first sentence is prevented from happening.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:53.166Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
